Cut 2026-10-19 on Anthony's word ("Keep pressing to release/tag v0.88.0. I'm headed to work and would like to use latest reflow2 there"), in PR #773 with the P3.5 fixes. A minor carrying:
- #770: a premise has a truth, honest proof readings, graph_report takes a budget;
- #771 (phase 2): reason_to_exist on a governed requirement, argued_by on SATISFIES/DEPENDS_ON, circular delivery;
- #772 (phase 3): statement_kind hypothesis and falsum, proofs by cases (cases, cases_exhaustive), cited results, open suppositions contest rather than refute, generalization over an open assumption's variable does not hold;
- #773: add_decision/add_requirement store the status given; every typed edge helper keeps what a redraw leaves out.

200 tools, as in 0.87.0; new arguments on add_inference, satisfies, depends_on and graph_report. THE SCHEMA STAMP MOVES (statement_kind gains two values): docs/upgrading-to-v0.88.0.md, measured with the published 0.87.0 binary — 0.87.0 refuses a store or export holding either value (even with --accept-newer), warns on one holding neither, and 0.88.0 opens a 0.87.0 store unchanged (same content hash). Nothing is deprecated or removed (deprecation::REGISTRY empty). Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019Xbw6PG9mXJiU2Sb421fnq
